  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through next Saturday)\nIssued at 1015 PM CDT Sat Aug 8 2026\n\nNot much change is anticipated for the start of the extended on \nMonday morning with the morphology/positioning of the upper level \nhigh largely static.  While there remains subtle differences in the \ndeterministic guidance, particularly with regards to the weakness in \nthe ridge to our east, things do not look good for much of change of \nweather until perhaps late week where POPs may edge up given the \nshifting of the high toward the east (yielding at least some monsoon \npotential) as a trough comes ashore the west coast.\n\nIt should be noted that we've just started downward on the mean high \ntemperature values based on seasonal averages.  Does this mean the \nheat is on its way down for good? No, not at all.  We can still get \n100+ degree temperatures well into September, but at least it's the \nfirst steps toward autumn.  The MJO just had a brief transit through \nphase 5 which could suggest some sort of front around the 25th of \nAugust.  It was a rather weak transit actually quickly shunting from \nphase 2 to phase 5 (both tending to suggest fronts about 21 days \nout) over the course of a couple days, but if you're looking for \nsome hope, there it is.",
